\begin_layout Standard
To debug an Alire-managed Ada project in VS Code install the Ada & SPARK and C/C++ extensions then configure tasks.json and launch.json to build with alr and debug with gdb.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Install Required Extensions
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Open VS Code Extensions (Ctrl+Shift+X) and install:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
• Ada & SPARK (AdaCore.ada):
 Provides language server support,
 syntax highlighting,
 and automatic Alire project detection.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
• C/C++ (ms-vscode.cpptools):
 Provides the cppdbg engine needed to drive GDB.
 (Note:
 On macOS with Apple Silicon you may need CodeLLDB instead of GDB depending on your toolchain).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Configure Alire & Open the Project
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Ensure that your Alire crate has a selected toolchain (e.g.,
 gnat_native and gprbuild).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
1.
 Open your Alire project folder in VS Code (File > Open Folder...).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
2.
 The Ada Language Server will automatically detect alire.toml and load your .gpr project environment.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
3.
 Open VS Code Settings (Ctrl+,),
 search for Allow Breakpoints Everywhere,
 and enable it ("debug.allowBreakpointsEverywhere":
 true) so you can place breakpoints on .adb files.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
3.
 Configure the Build Task (.vscode/tasks.json)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Create a .vscode/tasks.json file to compile your project with debug symbols using Alire before launching the debugger:
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
{
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
"version":
 "2.0.0",
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
"tasks":
 [
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
{
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
"label":
 "Alire Build (Debug)",
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
"type":
 "shell",
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
"command":
 "alr build --development",
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
"group":
 {
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
"kind":
 "build",
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
"isDefault":
 true
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
},
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
"problemMatcher":
 "$ada"
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
}
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
]
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
}
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
(Note:
 alr build defaults to development mode with -g debug symbols enabled in newer Alire versions,
 so --development ensures debug info is always included).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Configure the Debugger (.vscode/launch.json)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Create a .vscode/launch.json file to attach GDB to your compiled binary:
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
{
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
"version":
 "0.2.0",
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
"configurations":
 [
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
{
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
"name":
 "Debug Ada (Alire)",
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
"type":
 "cppdbg",
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
"request":
 "launch",
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
"program":
 "${workspaceFolder}/bin/your_executable_name",
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
"args":
 [],
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
"stopAtEntry":
 false,
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
"cwd":
 "${workspaceFolder}",
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
"environment":
 [],
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
"externalConsole":
 false,
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
"MIMode":
 "gdb",
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
"miDebuggerPath":
 "gdb",
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
"preLaunchTask":
 "Alire Build (Debug)",
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
"setupCommands":
 [
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
{
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
"description":
 "Enable pretty-printing for gdb",
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
"text":
 "-enable-pretty-printing",
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
"ignoreFailures":
 true
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
}
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
]
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
}
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
]
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
}
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Key Adjustments and Running
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Executable path:
 Replace your_executable_name in launch.json with your actual binary name (add .exe on Windows).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
GDB path:
 Because Alire manages toolchains in isolated paths,
 if VS Code reports that gdb cannot be found launch VS Code from an Alire-configured terminal (alr exec -- code .) or point "miDebuggerPath" directly to the gdb binary inside your Alire toolchain cache (~/.local/share/alire/toolchains/...).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Start debugging:
 Click the gutter next to a line number in your .adb file to set a breakpoint (F9) and press F5 to build and debug.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
For more details on advanced configurations,
 refer to the Ada & SPARK VS Code Extension User's Guide.
 [1] (https://docs.adacore.com/live/wave/als/html/vscode-extension-doc/index.html)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
GDB is not supported on Apple Silicon (ARM64) macOS
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Switch launch.json to Use LLDB
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
If using the standard Microsoft C/C++ extension (cppdbg) that AdaCore's extension relies on:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Open .vscode/launch.json in your project folder.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Change "MIMode" from "gdb" to "lldb".
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Remove "miDebuggerPath" (or leave it empty so VS Code finds lldb-mi automatically).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Add "targetArchitecture":
 "arm64" so it doesn't default to x86_64
\end_layout

